   164	### 2.8 F14/F15/M7 — crawler economics
   165	
   166	- `AssumeValid: true` on the crawler's `nostr.NewRelay` calls (firehose +
   167	  priority) + keep the single `CheckSignature` in `ingest` for new ids only.
   168	  Net: dupes cost 0 verifies (vs 1 today), new events cost 1 (vs 2), and the
   169	  ws read loop stops blocking on verify for replayed history.
   170	- Per-source high-water mark: remember last disconnect time; on reconnect use
   171	  `since = disconnectTime - overlap` (~1-6h). Full-history filter only on cold
   172	  start. (Dedup + priority sweeps cover stragglers; the full re-pull is what's
   173	  expensive, not a bounded re-pull.)
   174	- Worker pool for verify→enqueue ONLY if profiling shows one source saturating
   175	  a core — do `AssumeValid` first, it's free.
   176	- F18: `fetchOverlap` 24h → 1-2h (keep the daily full sweep as the safety net);
   177	  bounded parallel pubkey fetches (e.g. 4 workers); reuse one relay connection
   178	  per relay across the tick's pubkeys.
   179	
   180	### 2.9 F16/F17/M2/M6 — dedup & seen_events
   181	
   182	- `Dedup` keys → `map[[32]byte]struct{}` (hex-decode once): ~half the memory,
   183	  zero collision risk. Combined `CheckAndMark(id) bool` under one write lock;
   184	  `MarkMany` in `OnFlushed` under one lock instead of per-event.
   185	- `OnFlushed` → async: hand the batch to a dedicated goroutine via channel so
   186	  the SQLite txn never blocks the flush worker. Losing a `seen_events` write
   187	  only causes harmless re-ingest.
   188	- `seen_events`: bound by count, not age — prune by rowid
   189	  (`DELETE FROM seen_events WHERE rowid < (SELECT rowid FROM seen_events
   190	  ORDER BY rowid DESC LIMIT 1 OFFSET <cap>)`, cap ~4M) — no new index, O(deleted).
   191	  Optionally cut retention 7d→48h. Longer-term option: drop the table and warm
   192	  from CH (`WHERE received_at > now() - 1d`) — design decision, defer.
   193	
   194	### 2.10 F13/M13 — stats isolation & correctness
   195	
   196	- Followers rebuild into `author_follower_counts_staging` then
   197	  `EXCHANGE TABLES author_follower_counts AND author_follower_counts_staging`
   198	  (atomic; kills the 0-followers window).
   199	- Add `NOT dictHas('tombstone_dict', id)` to all refresh queries (M13).
   200	- Stats gets its own CH conn (§2.5). Consider stretching follower refresh to
   201	  15-30min or making it incremental if the kind-3 scan stays hot after §2.1.
   202	
   203	### 2.11 M1/M8/F19 — ops trivia (one-liners)
   204	
   205	- `/v1/health`: replace `count() FROM events_all` with
   206	  `SELECT sum(rows) FROM system.parts WHERE database=? AND table LIKE 'events_%' AND active`
   207	  (metadata-only) or drop the count entirely.
   208	- `http.Server`: `ReadHeaderTimeout: 10s`, `IdleTimeout: 120s`. No Read/WriteTimeout.
   209	- `config.example.yaml`: `batch.maxAge` 1s → 5s (match the production default;
   210	  the example currently reintroduces the small-parts anti-pattern).
   211	
   212	### 2.12 F6 (+M3, F11) — the one schema migration (defer, but design now)
   213	
   214	`tags_raw String` → `tags Array(Array(String))` with
   215	`tag_e/tag_p/tag_t/tag_d` as `MATERIALIZED` columns via `arrayMap/arrayFilter`.
   216	Kills: per-row JSON decode on reads (F6), per-event JSON marshal on writes
   217	(M3), the Go tag-extraction loop in `rowFromEvent`, and upgrades the
   218	arbitrary-tag fallback from `position(tags_raw, …)` substring scan to exact
   219	`arrayExists`. Backfill existing rows via `JSONExtract`. If index RAM
   220	measurement ever justifies it, bundle F11 (`FixedString(32)` ids) into the
   221	same one-time rewrite — otherwise skip F11.
   222	
   223	### 2.13 Deferred decisions (not scheduled)
   224	
   225	- **M9**: move kind 9735 to `social` tier (1y TTL) or add a `permanent` TTL —
   226	  product call; zap receipts may be the largest table long-term.
   227	- **Background replaceable compaction**: hourly/daily job tombstoning stale
   228	  permanent-tier versions in bulk — only after §2.3 lands, only if §2.1's
   229	  read-side collapse isn't enough and disk growth matters.
   230	- **FINAL evaluation**: FINAL today only collapses exact dupes (it does NOT
   231	  implement replaceable semantics — the `QueryEvents` comment is wrong). With
   232	  §2.1's `LIMIT 1 BY` machinery in place, test dropping `FINAL` from the
   233	  per-tier queries (`EXPLAIN` + a/b on a real dataset); big potential win on
   234	  wide scans. Keep `FINAL` on the F2 probe either way.
   235	- F11 (FixedString ids), F21 (limiter sharding) — do only with measurements.
   236	
   237	## 3. Phased implementation plan
   238	
   239	### P0 — crash/correctness fixes (small, do now)
   240	1. **F4 batcher rework** — pending/backoff/cap + M12 fixes. ~40 lines in
   241	   `batcher.go`. Acceptance: kill ClickHouse for 10 min under ingest; memory
   242	   stays flat, `ErrBatchFull` fires, recovery resumes without restart.
   243	2. **F1 read-side collapse** — `LIMIT 1 BY` in `QueryEvents` tail (+ `id ASC`
   244	   tiebreak). Acceptance: store 3 versions of a kind-3, REQ returns exactly the
   245	   newest; mixed-kind filters still return all regular events.
   246	3. **M1 health count** → `system.parts`. One line.
   247	4. **F19 server timeouts**. Two fields.
   248	5. **M8 config.example maxAge**. One line.
   249	
   250	### P1 — read path at scale
   251	6. **F8 default-since + `idx_pubkey` bloom index**; try `p_feed` projection,
   252	   keep iff `EXPLAIN` shows usage.
   253	7. **F12/M11 pool split + query semaphore** (write/read/stats conns, explicit
   254	   `MaxOpenConns`, bounded in-flight queries).
   255	8. **F2 slim replace probe** (two-column query).
   256	9. **F3 batched tombstones + debounced reload**. Acceptance: 100-tag kind-5
   257	   costs 1 dict reload, not 100.
   258	10. **F5/F7/F9/F10/F20** hygiene batch (one PR): select-columns, drop
   259	    `idx_content`, Debug log, fail-on-tier-error, REST clamps.
   260	
   261	### P2 — ingest economics
   262	11. **F15 `AssumeValid` + single verify**; measure; worker pool only if needed.
   263	12. **F14 per-source reconnect `since` HWM**.
   264	13. **F16 dedup `[32]byte` keys + `CheckAndMark`/`MarkMany`**; async `OnFlushed`.
   265	14. **F17/M2 rowid-bounded seen_events prune** (+retention cut to 48h).
   266	15. **F18 fetchOverlap→1-2h, bounded parallelism, conn reuse**.
   267	
   268	### P3 — stats correctness
   269	16. **F13 staging + EXCHANGE TABLES**, `dictHas` in refreshes, stats conn (from P1).
   270	
   271	### P4 — migration & product decisions (separate effort)
   272	17. **§2.12 native tags migration** (bundle F11 only if measured).
   273	18. **M9 9735 tier/TTL** product decision.
   274	19. Optional **bulk compaction job** for permanent tier (needs §2.3; also
   275	    decide dict RAM impact first — M5).
   276	20. **FINAL-removal experiment** once `LIMIT 1 BY` is proven in prod.
   277	
   278	## 4. Do NOT do
   279	
   280	| Tempting fix | Why it's wrong |
   281	|---|---|
   282	| Route crawler through `ReplaceEvent` | F2's cost × firehose rate; can't heal backlog anyway |
   283	| Drop-oldest when batcher overflows | Silent loss of ACKed client events; `ErrBatchFull` is the honest valve |
   284	| `uint64` dedup keys | Rare collision permanently loses an archive event |
   285	| `WriteTimeout`/`ReadTimeout` on http.Server | Kills long-lived WS subscriptions |
   286	| Parallel tier scans | 3× CH load per REQ under subscriber fan-out |
   287	| Reconstruct tags from `tag_e/p/t/d` columns | Loses markers, `amount`, `client`, and all non-accelerator tags |
   288	| Reorder PK to `(kind, created_at, …)` | Breaks the dominant `{kinds, authors}` path |
   289	| Age-based tombstone prune | Resurrects deleted permanent-tier events |
   290	| Hard-reject REQs without `since` | Breaks every `nak req -k 1`; inject a default instead |
   291	| Rely on LIFETIME alone for tombstone hide | 60s resurrection window is a delete-contract bug; debounce instead |
   292	| Hex→FixedString migration now | Compression already recovers most; bundle with the tags migration iff measured |
   293	
   294	## 5. Open questions for the maintainer
   295	
   296	1. **M9**: keep zap receipts in `permanent` forever, or move/retire them?
   297	2. **§2.4**: is a default `since` (e.g. 48h) acceptable relay behavior, or must
   298	   unbounded queries always be served? (Projection may make this moot.)
   299	3. **§2.9**: is durable `seen_events` worth keeping at all vs. warming dedup
   300	   from ClickHouse `received_at` at startup?

